cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Design Benchmark"
message: "If you use this data, please cite it and link the FontVibe article of the benchmark you used, e.g. https://fontvibe.ai/blog/gpt-6-1-terra-vs-claude-gemini-design-test."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "FontVibe"
    website: "https://fontvibe.ai"
abstract: >-
  Open data from FontVibe's benchmarks of AI models doing design work with
  text. 2026-10-llm-designer: eight language models (GPT-6.1 Terra, GPT-5.6
  Terra, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Luna, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Gemini 4
  Argon, Gemini 3.8 Flash) act as the designer in a fixed design pipeline, on 12
  briefs in four layers and six languages, three runs each, 287 designs scored
  blind. Two image-model benchmarks (Grok Imagine 2.0, Qwen Image 3.0) compare
  text rendering on ten design jobs. Every brief, output, image link, score and
  written reason is included, with scripts that recompute the published tables.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - graphic design
  - typography
  - text-to-image
  - evaluation
  - AI design
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://fontvibe.ai/blog/gpt-6-1-terra-vs-claude-gemini-design-test"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Funovate-Technology/ai-design-benchmark"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
